{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The sons of Levi.</b> He mentioned these two tribes first because they are older than Levi, for Levi is the principal matter — for he did not come now except to trace the lineage of Moses and Aaron, and he mentioned Gershon, Kehath, and Merari in the order they were born, when they went down to Egypt:" "\"He is Aaron and Moses.\" He put Aaron's name first because of his two sons, and he mentioned Levi's years of life but did not mention the years of the tribes, for the honor of Moses and Aaron:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:09.699493880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}